# The repo root IS the project directory.
#
# It previously used a whitelist rooted at $HOME (`/*` then re-admit patterns),
# because the repo had been initialised in the home directory alongside ~81GB
# of unrelated data. That was treating the symptom: the whitelist silently
# excluded every new directory, and the entire tekdromo package went uncommitted
# without any warning. Rooting the repo at the project fixes the cause.
#
# Rule of thumb for anything added below: ignore it only if it is GENERATED or
# REFETCHABLE. Never ignore something a fresh clone needs and cannot recreate -
# see the "large models" note for how that failure presents.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
# Virtualenvs. This runs against the system Python 3.6 on the target board, but
# contributors develop against a venv on a laptop - most of the suite needs no
# hardware at all.
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# -------------------------------------------------------- test / tooling ----
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ------------------------------------------------- generated by this app ----
# Rendered output, screen captures and A/B frames. Everything tools/ and
# tests/ writes lands here.
tek_out/
# Derived geometry cache, keyed by a hash of the source. Rebuilt on demand
# (~4s) and invalid the moment the field equation changes.
*.npz
# Left by tools/check_boot.sh, panic_screen.py and the profilers.
*.log
perf.data*

# ------------------------------------------------------------ large models --
# All three are refetchable, and all three are too large for git. A fresh clone
# has none of them - see README "Install".
#
# NOTE the failure mode, because it is quiet: with models/lbfmodel.yaml absent,
# Tracker._facemark() returns None rather than raising, so landmark fitting, the
# HUD face panel, and the EYE ALIGNMENT that recognition depends on all switch
# themselves off with no error anywhere. If recognition is inexplicably poor on
# a new checkout, check that file exists before anything else.
#
#   voices/   Piper voices, ~61MB each          -> tools/fetch_voice.sh
#   models/   Vosk STT ~68MB, lbfmodel.yaml ~54MB
#   lib/      side-loaded libstdc++ for vosk; a distro binary, not ours to
#             vendor. See tekdromo/voice/stt.py.
voices/
models/
lib/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- secrets ----
# Nothing here reads any of these today. They are listed so that the first
# person to add an API key does not have to remember to - this is a PUBLIC repo.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
credentials.json

# ------------------------------------------------------- local overrides ----
# Runtime state and per-user config live in ~/.config/tekdromo and
# ~/.cache/tekdromo, deliberately OUTSIDE the repo: the face gallery, people.md,
# people.json and the chosen voice are personal data and must not be committable
# by accident. These two are for anything local that does land in the tree.
*.local
local/

# ---------------------------------------------------------- editors / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sw[op]
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
